+When a user-agent review completes with findings resolved, the controller selects that patch-agent
+session and appends a feature-done confirmation prompt. A `yes` response records the user reply,
+marks the feature done, and closes the patch-agent session for frontend presentation. A `no` response
+records the user reply and reopens the session without sending a prompt to the backend. Any other
+message at the confirmation prompt reopens the session and continues through the normal send path.
+A follow-up message sent to an already closed patch-agent session reopens that session before the
+message is sent.
+
 The command transcript is also the conversation history for the persistent `command-agent`. That
